sxml transform - Run an XSLT 4.0 transformation

Usage: sxml transform [--initial-mode=NAME] [--initial-template=NAME] [--method=METHOD] [--param=NAME=VALUE]... STYLESHEET [INPUT]

Compiles the XSLT 4.0 stylesheet in STYLESHEET and transforms INPUT:
templates are applied to it in the initial mode (--initial-mode, else
the default mode), or --initial-template is called with it as the
focus. Without INPUT the initial template (--initial-template, else
xsl:initial-template) is called without a focus. The principal result
is written to standard output as the stylesheet's xsl:output says;
--method replaces the method. --param=NAME=VALUE binds the stylesheet
parameter $NAME to xs:untypedAtomic(VALUE). xsl:message output goes to
standard error. Modules and documents are read from local files only;
result documents with an href are not written. An error is reported
on standard error as STYLESHEET:LINE:COLUMN: err:CODE: description and
exits 1; an unreadable file exits 3.

Options:
  -h, --help                   Show this help and exit
      --initial-mode=NAME      Mode whose template rules process INPUT, instead of the default mode
      --initial-template=NAME  Named template to call, instead of applying templates to INPUT
      --method=METHOD          Serialization method of the result, replacing the stylesheet's (one of: adaptive, xml, xhtml, html, text, json)
      --param=NAME=VALUE       Bind stylesheet parameter $NAME to xs:untypedAtomic(VALUE) (repeatable)

Arguments:
  STYLESHEET  File holding the principal stylesheet module
  INPUT       XML document to transform, the global context item; - reads standard input

Examples:
  sxml transform style.xsl books.xml
  sxml transform --param=title=Books style.xsl books.xml
  sxml transform --initial-template=main report.xsl
  sxml transform --method=text --initial-mode=index style.xsl -
